- op: create  # decc
  at: '2026-08-22T00:09:32Z'  # decc
  by: agent  # decc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # decc
  clock: 1  # decc
  nonce: decc  # decc
  data:  # decc
    kind: invariant  # decc
    title: "is_likely_minified heuristic 3 has no comment anchor: a file whose docstring MENTIONS generated code is classified DERIVED and silently loses every symbol (2 of 3 on hypergumbo itself)"  # decc
    status: violated  # decc
    priority: 1  # decc
    parent:  # decc
    tags:  # decc
    - supply_chain  # decc
    - tier_filter  # decc
    - false_positive  # decc
    - two_homes  # decc
    isbefore: []  # decc
    duplicate_of: []  # decc
    not_duplicate_of: []  # decc
    pr_ref:  # decc
    description: "FOUND WHILE RE-PRICING WI-fozoh's COLLAPSE FOR INV-rozob, 2026-08-21, on hypergumbo's\nOWN repository at dev bbd1635dcc. Two hand-written first-party test files contribute\nZERO nodes to a default survey:\n\n    packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_spec_linker_count.py   0 nodes\n    packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_scip_generated.py      0 nodes\n    packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_ir.py                186 nodes  <- control\n\nThe two are not generated. What they have in common is a DOCSTRING that mentions some\nOTHER file being generated:\n\n    test_spec_linker_count.py:4  \"``docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`` is regenerated by\n                                  ``scripts/generate-architecture`` and ...\"\n    test_scip_generated.py:4     \"``scip_pb2.py`` is auto-generated by\n                                  ``scripts/build-scip-proto`` from a ...\"\n\nMECHANISM. supply_chain.is_likely_minified heuristic 3:\n\n    head = \"\\n\".join(lines[:5])\n    if re.search(r\"(Generated by|@generated|DO NOT EDIT)\", head, re.IGNORECASE):\n        return True\n\nNo comment anchor, no word boundary, case-insensitive, and \"regenerated by\" contains\n\"generated by\" as a substring. The file is classified tier 4 (DERIVED) and the default\ntier filter drops every symbol it has.\n\n*** THE CAREFUL SIBLING IN THE SAME MODULE DOCUMENTS THIS EXACT HAZARD AND AVOIDS IT.\nsupply_chain._GENERATED_HEADER_PATTERN: \"The pattern is intentionally narrow: it\nrequires the phrase to sit on a comment line so we don't accidentally flag a file that\nmentions the word in prose.\" It flags 0 of these 2. ONE QUESTION, TWO HOMES, and the\nloose one silently wins -- and it wins because it runs in the tier pipeline while the\ncareful one feeds `is_generated`. ***\n\nAND THE MODULE ALREADY PAID FOR THIS ONCE, ON THE SIBLING HEURISTIC. The INV-lukop note\ndirectly above `is_likely_minified` gates heuristic 1 (average line length) to web\nextensions precisely because misclassifying \"classifies its whole file tier-4 (derived),\nand the default tier filter then drops EVERY symbol and edge for that file with no\ndiagnostic. Gating the heuristic to these extensions closes that silent-whole-file-drop\nvector; the @generated / sourcemap / webpack heuristics stay universal because they are\nlanguage-agnostic generation signals.\" Heuristic 3 IS one of the heuristics that note\nwaves through as safe, and it is not: it is language-agnostic about the MARKER and\nentirely un-anchored about WHERE the marker sits.\n\nWHAT THIS COSTS, and it is not only these two files. Any file whose first five lines\ndescribe generated code is dropped whole: documentation-adjacent tests, codegen tooling,\nand README-style module docstrings that explain what a build step emits. On hypergumbo\nitself that is 2 of 3 file-boundary anchors -- a 67% false-positive rate in that\npopulation -- and the drop is silent (nothing in analysis_incomplete or\nlimits.failed_files distinguishes it from a file that has no symbols).\n\nNOT MEASURED: the corpus-wide false-positive rate (the four upstream files I checked for\nINV-rozob -- 3 sqlalchemy, 1 poetry -- are all GENUINELY generated, so hypergumbo's own\nrepo is the only place I have counterexamples); whether `limits.tier_filtered_files`\n(WI-tulit) already names these, which would make the drop disclosed rather than silent\nand would change the severity but not the misclassification; and whether tightening\nheuristic 3 to require a comment anchor would lose any true positive currently caught\n(the Go convention `// Code generated by ... DO NOT EDIT.` is already comment-anchored,\nso the narrow pattern may be a drop-in)."  # decc
    fields:  # decc
      statement: "A file is classified as generated only on evidence about ITSELF; prose describing some other file's generation must not drop the mentioning file's symbols."  # decc
      root_cause: "supply_chain.is_likely_minified heuristic 3 searches (Generated by|@generated|DO NOT EDIT) case-insensitively over the first five lines with no comment anchor and no word boundary, so a docstring saying another file 'is regenerated by X' matches. The file becomes tier 4 (DERIVED) and the default tier filter drops all its symbols with no diagnostic. The module's own _GENERATED_HEADER_PATTERN answers the same question with a comment anchor precisely to avoid prose, and flags 0 of the observed false positives."  # decc
- op: discuss  # 74ad
